     "text": "{\"count\": 1, \"rationale\": \"Without defences, exfiltration is reachable: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user. pivot_internal gives reach_internal. auth_appserver gives foothold_appserver. kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin. auth_dc gives foothold_dc. escalate_dc gives admin_dc. dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin. auth_db then escalate_db gives admin_db, and exfiltrate_db succeeds. So zero controls is not enough. Both exfiltration paths (db and fileserver) need stolen_dbadmin. The only source of stolen_dbadmin is admin_dc, which needs foothold_dc. The only source of foothold_dc is auth_dc, which requires NOT mfa_admin. Deploying mfa:admin alone therefore blocks every path to exfiltration, so the minimum is 1.\"}"
